---
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
const faqs = [
  { q: "Can PDFSherpa unlock a PDF if I don’t know the password?", a: "No. Unlock PDF only works with the correct password. It does not guess or crack passwords." },
  { q: "Why remove a password I already know?", a: "So you don’t have to type it every time, and so you can merge, compress, sign or upload the file. Many portals reject protected PDFs." },
  { q: "Is the unlocked file safe to keep?", a: "It is no longer protected, so keep it on your own device and don’t forward it to people who shouldn’t read it." },
];
---
<GuideLayout slug="remove-password-from-pdf" faqs={faqs}>
<p><strong>Short answer:</strong> if you know the password, open <a href="/unlock-pdf">Unlock PDF</a>, select the file, type the password and click <strong>Unlock PDF</strong>. You download a copy that opens without a password.</p>

  <h2>Step by step</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="/unlock-pdf">pdfsherpa.com/unlock-pdf</a>.</li>
    <li>Select the protected PDF.</li>
    <li>Type the password that opens it. It is checked before anything else happens.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Unlock PDF</strong> and download the unlocked copy.</li>
  </ol>

  <AdSlot variant="inline" slot="guide-article" />

  <h2>Where these passwords usually come from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bank and card statements:</strong> banks often use a combination like part of your name and your date of birth. The email or letter from the bank explains the format.</li>
    <li><strong>Payslips:</strong> often your employee ID or date of birth. Ask your HR department.</li>
    <li><strong>Utility bills and tax documents:</strong> usually explained in the email that came with the PDF.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why upload portals reject protected PDFs</h2>
  <p>
    A portal cannot read, check or compress a file it can’t open. If an upload fails with an error about a protected or encrypted file, unlock it first,
    upload it, and keep the protected original for your records.
  </p>

  <h2>What Unlock PDF won’t do</h2>
  <p>
    It won’t open a file without the right password and it won’t bypass restrictions set by someone else. If you’ve forgotten the password, ask
    whoever sent the document for a new copy.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>The password is checked and the file is decrypted in your browser. Neither is uploaded.</p>
</GuideLayout>
